---
import FadeIn from "./FadeIn.tsx";
import ValueProp from "./ValueProp.astro";
---

<div>
  <FadeIn client:visible>
    <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-center">
      I build MVPs that your future team can actually work&nbsp;in.
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed text-center max-w-2xl mx-auto">
      I'm a software engineer with 5+ years building production apps in React,
      Node.js, and PostgreSQL. Here's what I deliver:
    </p>
  </FadeIn>

  <FadeIn client:visible>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-5 md:gap-6 mt-12">
      <ValueProp title="Clean, modular architecture">
        <svg
          slot="icon"
          xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
          width="22"
          height="22"
          viewBox="0 0 24 24"
          fill="none"
          stroke="currentColor"
          stroke-width="1.5"
          stroke-linecap="round"
          stroke-linejoin="round"
          class="text-teal-300"
          ><rect x="3" y="3" width="7" height="7"></rect><rect
            x="14"
            y="3"
            width="7"
            height="7"></rect><rect x="3" y="14" width="7" height="7"
          ></rect><rect x="14" y="14" width="7" height="7"></rect></svg
        >
        Component structure, API design, and database schemas that make sense to
        the next developer who touches the code. No spaghetti, no duct tape.
      </ValueProp>

      <ValueProp title="Security from day one">
        <svg
          slot="icon"
          xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
          width="22"
          height="22"
          viewBox="0 0 24 24"
          fill="none"
          stroke="currentColor"
          stroke-width="1.5"
          stroke-linecap="round"
          stroke-linejoin="round"
          class="text-teal-300"
          ><path
            d="M20 13c0 5-3.5 7.5-7.66 8.95a1 1 0 0 1-.67-.01C7.5 20.5 4 18 4 13V6a1 1 0 0 1 1-1c2 0 4.5-1.2 6.24-2.72a1.17 1.17 0 0 1 1.52 0C14.51 3.81 17 5 19 5a1 1 0 0 1 1 1z"
          ></path></svg
        >
        Proper authentication, input validation, environment-based secrets
        management, and role-based access control. Not afterthoughts — defaults.
      </ValueProp>

      <ValueProp title="Built to scale">
        <svg
          slot="icon"
          xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
          width="22"
          height="22"
          viewBox="0 0 24 24"
          fill="none"
          stroke="currentColor"
          stroke-width="1.5"
          stroke-linecap="round"
          stroke-linejoin="round"
          class="text-teal-300"
          ><polyline points="22 12 18 12 15 21 9 3 6 12 2 12"></polyline></svg
        >
        Optimized queries, proper caching strategies, and infrastructure choices
        that won't bankrupt you when traffic spikes.
      </ValueProp>

      <ValueProp title="Tested and documented">
        <svg
          slot="icon"
          xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
          width="22"
          height="22"
          viewBox="0 0 24 24"
          fill="none"
          stroke="currentColor"
          stroke-width="1.5"
          stroke-linecap="round"
          stroke-linejoin="round"
          class="text-teal-300"
          ><path
            d="M14 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z"
          ></path><polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8"></polyline><line
            x1="16"
            y1="13"
            x2="8"
            y2="13"></line><line x1="16" y1="17" x2="8" y2="17"></line></svg
        >
        Enough test coverage and documentation that your first hire can onboard
        in days, not weeks.
      </ValueProp>
    </div>
  </FadeIn>
</div>
